{{ToonInfo|Toon=Scraps|extra=Paper Craft|Pronoun=She|Date=June 14th, 2024|type=Single}}

==Appearance==
Scraps is a yellow paper craft that resembles a paper origami cat. Her head is flat-ish hexagonal with pointed, salmon-colored ears that each have a vertical fold down the middle. She has two vertical, stick-like or scar-like darkish salmon-colored lines under her eyes that are fully visible when they are shut. She wears a white dress resembling an upside-down cupcake liner and has a tail poking through it. Her tail is yellow, thin, and has a darkish salmon-colored solo cup with white lining at the tip. On each of her limbs, she has round salmon-colored paws with three sharp darkish salmon-colored claws and a clawed thumb on both of her hand paws.

==Personality==
Scraps is a kind and artistic [[Toon]] who loves making arts & crafts and cares about the well-being of the other Toons, especially her younger brother, {{CI|Goob|name=true}}. She is sometimes airheaded and forgets to do things, such as in her interactions with {{CI|Brightney|name=true}} and {{CI|Tisha|name=true}}. She also looks for multiple ways to get materials for her art, such as with {{CI|Blot|name=true}} for his ink and even asked {{CI|Sprout|name=true}} about using ketchup as an alternative (to which both have refused to that). Despite not quite being a cat, she has many tendencies of one, such as liking yarn, hissing in some of her dialogues, getting on all fours when startled, liking fish, disliking water (though this may also be due to her being made of paper), and wagging her tail when annoyed or angry. She also may get somewhat aggressive and act a bit immature in some situations, such as in her interactions with {{CI|Pebble|name=true}} and another with {{CI|Shrimpo|name=true}}. She also may have a slight grudge towards Shrimpo, as she mentions him in her interactions with {{CI|Boxten|name=true}} and {{CI|Flyte|name=true}}.

Overall, she is a mature Toon for the most part and cares about her brother, Goob, making sure that she is there for him.

