==Requirement Strategies==
*For the first requirement, focus on picking up [[Research Capsules]] and extracting [[Machines]]. The Machine and Capsule count increases the further you descend, so you can earn more {{II|Ichor|name=true}}.
*For the second requirement, have a Distractor [[Toon]] bring {{CI|Twisted Goob|name=true}} to the elevator to you so you can get aggro. Playing as {{CI|Rodger|name=true}} also helps you get Research faster because of his Passive [[Ability]]. This will be easier if Twisted Goob is on the [[Daily Twisted Board]].

==Strategies==
Scraps possesses the best Stamina stat in the game (tied with {{CI|Sprout|name=true}}, {{CI|Bobette|name=true}}, and {{CI|Blot|name=true}}) and an [[Ability]] that has the potential to help her escape from [[Twisteds]] or to quickly get to the [[Elevator]] during [[Panic Mode]] or get to Machines faster—granted there's another [[Toon]] or [[Machine]] nearby. These traits make her best suited to Survival. While her below-average [[Movement Speed]] does partially negate her large Stamina pool, [[Items]] like {{II|Speed Candy}}Speed Candies or {{II|Box o' Chocolates}}Boxes o' Chocolates and [[Trinkets]] such as {{TI|Pink Bow|name=true}} are more than capable of turning her into a force to be reckoned with. Otherwise, she doesn't excel at anything in particular.

Hovering your mouse over nearby Toons on PC or being in their proximity on Mobile can quickly identify players or Machines with a white outline to grapple onto them. This is useful for noticing teammates through walls, but remember that her {{AI|Scraps|name=true}} Ability requires line of sight, however, if the target moves behind an object, you will continue to move to their location when you had initially grappled anyways. This could also work on Machines, but it is less efficient as you cannot rely on Machines to spawn in the right spots every run and grappling on Machines should more often than not be used if planning to extract them, but it is still a helpful tool. On later Floors, where Machine count increases, escape becomes easier due to the abundance of things to grapple onto. However, do keep in mind that in [[Blackouts]], there may be Twisteds near the Machine that may hit you right after using your Ability due to its slight endlag. It also takes about ~0.8 seconds for you to move towards the Machine after activating the Ability, so a bit of distance if you are being chased is welcome.

While she does have 5{{Star}} Stamina, her 2 Star Movement Speed can conflict a lot, making her only outrun the Twisteds by a little bit as well as making it hard to lose sight of them. It is heavily recommended to use Run Speed Trinkets such as Pink Bow (24.2 run speed), {{TI|Speedy Shoes|name=true}} (23.125 run speed). With this, she can have lots of Stamina to run as well as having enough Run Speed to get away. Using {{TI|Clown Horn|name=true}}/{{TI|Ribbon Spool|name=true}} together is also good, but it will take both of your Trinket slots, though it comes at the benefit of 24.75 Run Speed, almost 3 Star Run Speed. Though, if you still want a Trinket slot open for something else, Pink Bow would probably be the best option out of these in terms of consistency. {{TI|Ghost Snakes In A Can|name=true}} can also be a good choice, especially in later Floors where more Machines spawn, allowing for even quicker travel across Floors, and taking advantage of the invincibility frames more often through her Ability, though it doesn't directly boost her Movement Speed, only general traversal.

One niche Scraps is very good at is passing Twisteds to distractors, primarily coming down to her average Stealth and Ability. Since the most common distractor choices have 2 or 3 Stars in Stealth, she can easily pass Twisteds to them. When passing to 3 Star Toons, she can bring the Twisted towards their distraction area or near the distractor directly, before grappling to a faraway Machine or player, thus swapping the distance priority. Due to her invincibility frames while grappling, this can also allow her to pass faster Twisteds and ranged Twisteds more safely. When passing to 2 Star Stealth Toons, she could instead opt to grapple directly to the distractor. If she has {{TI|Diary|name=true}} equipped, she can use this exact strategy for 3 Star Stealth distractors as well. When combined with a Movement Speed increase from an Item or Trinket (such as Pink Bow), and her 5 Star Stamina, she can pass practically any Twisted to a distractor. This may not be applicable with a distractor who has 4+ Stars in Stealth, but she could possibly bring the Twisteds to the distractor, followed by U-turning around a corner or island by grappling. Although {{CI|Glisten|name=true}} and {{CI|Flutter|name=true}} could theoretically outdo her with this, thanks to their higher speeds, and Glisten's teleportation through walls, both of them don't get invincibility frames with their Abilities, have longer cooldowns, and Glisten has lower Stealth.

Since Scraps' Ability gives her invincibility frames while she's grappling, it does allow her to make certain moves that many other Toons can't. She can bait or pass by long-ranged Twisteds ({{CI|Twisted Goob|name=true}} and {{CI|Twisted Scraps|name=true}}) without having to hide behind cover, since she could just grapple to a Machine/player. She can quickly leave the ranges of {{CI|Twisted Rodger|name=true}} and {{CI|Twisted Razzle & Dazzle|name=true}}, though the 2 Star Movement Speed could still be an issue. She can also pass straight through {{CI|Twisted Blot|name=true}}'s hands and {{CI|Twisted Sprout|name=true}}'s tendrils. Keep in mind that these do require a Machine or other Toon that is close enough to be in range.

Scraps isn't the best Toon for completing [[Dyle's Floor]]; her lower mobility and [[Skill Check]] both pose large disadvantages, as she will struggle to get away from Twisteds (though this is somewhat mitigated by her [[Stamina]] [[stat]]) and her 2 Star Skill Check could put you at risk if you aren't good at hitting them, not to mention the +50 Stamina the Floor gives is really unnecessary for her. Though, she does have a niche at the same time, as the abundant amount of [[Machines]] scattered around the Floor can allow for quick traversal and escapes, thanks to her Ability's cooldown. If you struggle with survivability in terms of Movement Speed, [[Glisten]] may be a better alternative, as he has 3 Star Movement Speed and can extract much faster. His Ability's much longer cooldown, as well it not working on Machines, the 2 Star [[Stealth]] stat and shared Skill Check stat could make the switch kind of iffy.

If you want to enhance Scraps' Extraction, using {{TI|Vee's Remote|name=true}} is a great option as the Floor can progress faster. Her below-average extractability makes extracting quite difficult for her, so, if other extractors are present, ask them to do your Machine, and use the time saved to find other Machines or run to the Elevator before Panic Mode begins.

Note that Scraps' stat spread is quite medicore. 2 Star Skill Check coupled with 3 Star Extraction makes the extraction process a bit slow, and 2 Star Movement Speed makes her high Stamina less beneficial (being able to run for longer won't help if you can't outrun a fast Twisted like {{CI|Twisted Pebble|name=true}}). While these weaknesses can be mitigated with Trinkets and awareness, Scraps is generally overshadowed by most Toons who can extract faster and possess even better survival. Scraps' main advantage over others is her Stamina, but Stamina isn't a good stat to invest Stars in due to both Well-Paced and Endurance cards giving 20 Stamina and TIMES UP with 50, adding up to almost 3 extra Stars in Stamina. Additionally, though Scraps can traverse faster via Crafty Grapple, one may be better off with higher movement speed instead.

