==Trivia==
*In [[Changelog|v0.7.1]], Scraps' [[Ability]] {{AI|Scraps|name=true}} was buffed to allow her to grab onto [[Machines]] as well, instead of just [[Toons]].
**In that update, a bug where grappling onto a Toon moving behind an object made her Ability fail and make her stuck was patched.
*Scraps is {{CI|Goob|name=true}}'s older sister.
*There was a Scraps [[Introduction Card]] under the [[Elevator]] in-game, used for the arrows to know where to point during [[Panic Mode]].
*Though her appearance is cat-like, she has stated that she isn't an actual cat and just has a feline appearance.
**Despite this, Scraps claims to have an appetite for fish (which can be seen in a dialogue with {{CI|Finn|name=true}}) and hisses in some lines of dialogue (one with {{CI|Shrimpo|name=true}}, one with {{CI|Pebble|name=true}} and one with {{CI|Eclipse|name=true}} [as she made her hiss on purpose]).
***She also likes yarn, as stated in {{CI|Tisha|name=true}}'s dialogue, which can be seen in her room—a common stereotype for cats.
***Similar to a real cat, her tail wags/thrashes when she's annoyed or angry, as shown in her interaction with {{CI|Looey|name=true}}.
****Seen in an animation with {{CI|Vee|name=true}}, her tail might give a small swish if she's happy/excited.
***In an animation, she jumps on the buzzer scared when [[Vee]] appears next to her, with her pose being similar to how cats react when they are scared by something in cartoons.
*Her name, Scraps, is a term used to describe small, leftover pieces of materials, especially taken from a bigger piece. This name may have been given to her due to her being a paper craft, which are usually made from scraps of paper.
**Her cobbled-together appearance may also be a reason for this name, being a mixture of materials rather than just one type (paper, plastic cup, crayon, etc).
**Another reason for this name could be that Scraps is a feline-like name.
*Scraps does not mind {{CI|Dandy|name=true}}, but wants him to not let [[Pebble]] into the [[Elevator]], as stated in one of her interactions with Pebble.
*Scraps has apparently won every prize [[Vee]] has given away on her show by giving lucky guesses for every answer.
**This implies that Scraps can be very lucky, which is mentioned in an interaction with Vee. Cats are often tied to luck, which is likely the source of this trait.
*In [[Roleplaying Mode]], Scraps shares the same room with [[Goob]] because they are siblings.
*Scraps is designation '''SC-015''', with the '''SC''' standing for Side Character.
**Despite being older than [[Goob]], Goob was oddly created before Scraps.
*Scraps is the first non-[[Main Character]] [[Toon]] to have 5{{Star}} on a [[Stat]].
**She was the only one to have it up until [[Changelog|v0.3]].
*If Scraps and [[Goob]] use their [[Abilities]] on each other simultaneously, they will cancel out and the Scraps doesn't move.
**If 2 Scraps use their Abilities on each other, they meet up in the middle.
*[[Goob]] and Scraps have a similar [[Ability]], with Goob's letting him drag [[Toons]] toward him, and Scraps being able to drag herself towards Toons.
*The magenta lines over Scraps' eyes are actually crayon makeup.
**It is also likely that her [[Trinket]], {{TI|Crayon Set|name=true}}, was used to draw the lines.
*Scraps was originally male in old concept art, being visible in some posters where she has no eyelashes and missing spaces between pronouns on her info card.<ref>https://discord.com/channels/969934252844138496/1251545388259741768/1266027125719302185</ref>
**She is not canonically transgender, however.
*Scraps was originally not going to be [[Goob]]'s sister when [[Qwel]] was designing her.<ref>https://discord.com/channels/969934252844138496/1251545388259741768/1305307327943016569</ref> But this was changed since Qwel thought it'd be a nice connection, and put the two together as siblings, mostly given that they're both crafts.<ref>https://discord.com/channels/969934252844138496/1251545388259741768/1305307423707500584</ref>
*Originally, Scraps was not intended to be cat-like. Her 'cat ears' were initially intended on being horns, but they resembled cat ears strongly enough that [[Qwel]] decided to cave in with the cat look.
**In a QnA stream, Qwel referred to Scraps' ears as horns on accident.
**This might explain why [[Shrimpo]] says "{{Text|AND I DON'T LIKE YOUR EAR, HORN, THINGYS!!}}" in one of his dialogues with her.
*Scraps would be nervous if someone else is watching her draw, as confirmed by [[Qwel]] in a New Years QnA stream.
*Due to a bug after the [[2024 Christmas Event]], her {{Skin|Cutesy Calico}} [[Skin]] was completely removed from [[Dandy's Store]]. This bug was fixed and the skin returned later in a patch.
*There was a bug where her {{Skin|Cutesy Calico}} [[Skin]] had no right foot on June 25, 2025. This was fixed shortly after.
*Prior to [[Changelog|v0.26.1]], Scraps and [[Vee]] had the longest interaction in the game, with 7 lines.
**This dialogue is now the second-longest, with the longest ones being [[Brusha]]'s dialogues with [[Rodger]] and {{CI|Toodles|name=true}}, with 8 lines each.
*Scraps has acrophobia (fear of heights) seen in her interaction with {{CI|Flutter|name=true}}.
**This is rather ironic considering her feline nature, since most cats instinctually seek higher ground and are able to withstand greater fall damage.
*Despite her head being a hexagon, in the storyboard for Season 2, Episode 8, her head is an octagon, very likely a mistake.
*In Scraps' dialogue with {{CI|Brusha|name=true}}, it seems Scraps believes Brusha's art isn't as real as her own art, as seen between the dialogue between the two. It also seems as if the two aren't on good terms as Brusha calls Scraps 'Glitter Glue painting'.
*Scraps is one of the few [[Toons]] to actually fight back against [[Shrimpo]]'s bullying, albeit with hissing, with {{CI|Connie|name=true}} and [[Pebble]] being the only other Toons to fight back.
*Scraps, [[Goob]], and {{CI|Brightney|name=true}} are the last Toons to get optimized.
*Strangely, Scraps lacks eyelashes when she blinks, though this only applies to her Default Skin. This is very likely an editing mistake.
*Scraps is the first [[Toon]] to have ears, the second being [[Looey]], the third being {{CI|Rudie|name=true}}, the fourth being {{CI|Cocoa|name=true}}, and the fifth being [[Eclipse]].
*Scraps is currently the only playable [[Toon]] with 5{{Star}} [[Stamina]] to not have 2 Star [[Extraction Speed]], excluding {{CI|Dyle|name=true}} and [[Dandy]] since they are both developer exclusive.
*Scraps' {{Skin|Cutesy Calico}} [[Skin]] was replaced by the {{Skin|Crafty Calico}} Skin for an unknown reason in [[Changelog|v0.20.1]].
*Scraps is the first [[Toon]] to have a redesigned [[Skin]] along with [[Flutter]]'s {{Skin|Vivid Monarch}} Skin.
*When using Scraps' [[Ability]] over an [[Ichor Leak]] puddle, you will still be inflicted with the {{Debuff|Illness|III}} and {{Debuff|Slow|I}}.
*Scraps' {{Skin|Wicked Stitch}} [[Skin]] appears to be a reference to the "magical girl" archetype in Japanese fantasy media. Her tail in particular resembles the staff/wand that such a character typically wields.

